Package: riscos-support
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: dosfstools
Recommends: riscos-risc3d, riscos-print
Conflicts: systemd-sysv, sysvinit-core
Breaks: riscos-harddisc (<< 1.0.0060-1)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-rolpkg
Description: The Linux side of RISC OS on Linux
 What runs RISC OS on Linux: init, rol-fb (screen, keyboard and mouse),
 rol-snd (sound), rol-netd (network and Wi-Fi), rol-cmd (Linux commands
 for RISC OS, with the root password), rol-usbd (USB devices for RISC
 OS), QEMU for machines that can't run 32-bit code (qemu-arm-riscos),
 rol-print (RISC OS's print jobs to Linux's CUPS), NativeSupport, and
 this repository's source and key. A restart puts a new version to use.
 Recommends riscos-risc3d, so that RISC OS programs can draw with the GPU
 (RISC3D), and riscos-print, so that RISC OS can print, with nothing else
 to install. Conflicts with systemd-sysv and sysvinit-core: init here is
 its own. Depends on
 dosfstools: start-up checks the FAT (boot) partition and repairs it.
